    "description": "1. Decide on the closed-loop pole locations. 2. Choose a desired pair of dominant second-order poles. 3. Select the rest of the poles to have real parts corresponding to sufficiently damped modes. 4. Ensure zeros are far enough into the LHP to avoid appreciable effect on second-order behavior. 5. Use a function like acker with A and B to find the control gains.",
